# Project Overview

npm-workspaces monorepo: `server`, `client`, `admin`, `e2e`.

| Workspace | Stack | Port |
|-----------|-------|------|
| `server` | Express 4 (CommonJS, plain JS) + PostgreSQL 16 via `pg` | 5000 |
| `client` | Next.js 16, Pages Router, React 18, TypeScript | 3000 |
| `admin` | Vite 6 + React 18 + react-router-dom 6, TypeScript | 5173 |
| `e2e` | Playwright | — |

## Commands

- Install: `npm install` (root)
- Dev: `npm run dev -w server`, `npm run dev -w client`, `npm run dev -w admin`
- Test: `npm run test -w server`, `npm run test -w client`, `npm run test -w admin`
- Migrate: `npm run migrate -w server`
- Seed: `npm run seed -w server`

## Multilingual

Three locales: `ru` (default), `en`, `am`. Multilingual DB fields use `*_ru`, `*_en`, `*_am` suffixes. Client translations live in `client/public/locales/{ru,en,am}/common.json` via `next-i18next`.

## API Response Contract

All endpoints return `{ ok: true, ...data }` on success or `{ ok: false, error: { message, details? } }` on failure. Both `client/lib/api.ts` and `admin/src/api.ts` share this `ApiResponse<T>` type.

## Content Model

DB-backed content blocks (`content_blocks` table) are keyed by `(page_name, section_name)`. Content schemas are defined in **both** `server/src/contentSchemas/` (JS) and `admin/src/contentSchemas/` (TS) and must stay in sync.
